* rtc: the real-time clock, 0014 and 072.
* The reference model cannot predict a clock, so this test checks itself
* and runs on the RTL only.  In monitor mode the clock is set to a value
* and read twice: both readings must be at or above that value, the second
* above the first, and no more than 1000 (decimal) clock periods later.
* Then the clock is cleared (j = 0) and must read small again.
         INCLUDE "rt_direct.cal"
         TBEGIN
         S1      KSET,0
         RT      S1                      ; 0014: clock = (S1)
         S2      RT                      ; 072
         S3      RT
         S0      S2-S1
         JSP     OK1
         TFAIL   2                       ; first reading below the value set
OK1      S0      S3-S2
         JSN     OK2
         TFAIL   3                       ; the clock did not move
OK2      JSP     OK3
         TFAIL   4                       ; the clock went backwards
OK3      S4      D'1000
         S5      S3-S2
         S0      S4-S5
         JSP     OK4
         TFAIL   5                       ; two readings too far apart
OK4      RT      S0                      ; j = 0: clear the clock
         S2      RT
         S4      D'1000
         S0      S4-S2
         JSP     OK5
         TFAIL   6                       ; the clock was not cleared
OK5      TPASS
         TEND
KSET     CON     X'0000123456789ABC
         END
